{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1023034-w20-kinfetch-and-garou","id":1023034,"title":"[W20] Kinfetch and Garou","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T17:08:46-08:00","id":1023034,"title":"[W20] Kinfetch and Garou","content":"(I'm visiting family and on my phone, so forgive the grammar errors) <br /> <br /> From my readings, a Kinfetch is assign to a child via ritual. However, in W20 the ritual that detects a future Garou registers unchanged garou as kinfolk. Thus there is a gap between assigning Kinfetch to known garou. <br /> <br /> I want to run the following idea to bridge this gap. Most children born to garou/ known kinfolk are assigned a Kinfetch. The Kinfetch will follow the child around and if the child shows signs of a coming first change, it will go back to the Sept the child was born to. A Kinfetch will eventually grow bored and leave a kinfolk in thier early twenties. Sometimes a Kinfetch will grow bored and leave sooner, which may cause problems. <br /> <br /> In the end times, garou do not have time to assign Kinfetches to all thier children, so some cubs may become lost. Or perhaps assigning a Kinfetch could be something a trusted kinfolk could do? Maybe religions already have ceremonies celebrating a birth of a child. It would be easy to hide a Kinfetch ritual in one of these. <br /> <br /> Any holes in my idea?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T19:20:03-08:00","id":1023069,"title":"","content":"My impression from back in the day had been that you couldn't tell pre-Change Garou from Kin unless you were a Silver Fang using the Baptism of Fire to attach a Kin-Fetch to the kid and that nobody else had any strong notions who would change and who wouldn't. This does not appear to mesh with anyone else's reading, but I think it fits the flavor of the game better. Your idea seems quite workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T21:40:39-08:00","id":1023105,"title":"","content":"One problem that I remember with using a Kinfetch is that there are servants of the Wyrm that can detect it and will home in on the person that it is protecting. I would think that the principle reason to not use a Kinfetch on Human Kinfolk is to allow them to blend into the larger human population. Instead, Garou (and Fera) would keep a mundane eye on things from a distance and would step in when the person experienced the First Change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:59:19-08:00","id":1023348,"title":"","content":"Your process sounds coherent. The extent to which how many children born of Garou and kinfolk undergo the Rite of Baptism of Fire depends on the tribe. Silver Fangs probably utilize it the most since they keep track of their lineage much more closely. I imagine very few Bone Gnawers use it, and those that do are limited to a handful of children born to Garou themselves. The rest fall somewhere inbetween on the spectrum.<br /> <br /> Note that the description of the Scent of True Form Gift does not completely preclude identification of pre-Change Garou. The statement that they smell like Kin is attached to the statement that Garou with the Gift <i>automatically</i> smell Kinfolk and Garou. In all other cases, they roll. So it may just be that the Gift does not automatically and always detect pre-Change Garou; it is not infallible. While pre-Change Garou are not listed in the success results, it's possible to argue that they can be detected with a high enough search result - perhaps the two successes generally needed for most supernatural creatures, but perhaps more. So while normally they detect as Kin, it may be possible to determine that yes, they are Garou. Use of the Gift is not automatically useful, but it can help whittle down the odds. Certainly as a house rule it seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:40:43-08:00","id":1023694,"title":"","content":"How close do you have to be to automatically detect them? Could you sense them by just walking into the same stadium or mall? If so, it would be easy to keep tabs on the Human Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T21:25:08-08:00","id":1024103,"title":"","content":"Scent of True Form is supposed to be an actual smell. So if you can smell them and tie them into that one specific person, then you know (or at least you can roll to see if you know).<br /> <br /> This would mean that depending where you are, it might be better to be in lupus form than homid since a lupus smelling sense is much better. So if you are in the wilderness, a Garou with the Gift in lupus form will likely quickly learn what kinds of creatures are out there, at least if they are downwind. Lupus likely won't be in a shopping mall, so the Garou in homid form will need to be quite close - I'd rule around the same distance they could pick up tobacco smoke smell from someone's clothes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}